\section{Normalization and value columns}{

Each endpoint is normalized per plate against \code{denom}, the median of the
plate's VC wells (on the transformed scale, if any). Defaults, as
published:
\itemize{
\item Total Distance, \code{"log_diff"}: \code{(log10(x + 1) - denom) * 100}, with
\code{denom} the VC median of \code{log10(x + 1)}.
\item Distance Change/Shift, \code{"none"}: used as is (already relative to
the VC curve).
\item Movement Similarity, \code{"ratio"}: \code{x / denom * 100 - 100}.
}
\code{"log_ratio"}, \code{(log10(x) - denom) / denom * 100} with \code{denom} the VC
median of \code{log10(x)}, is an older alternative.
The output keeps three values per row: \code{endpoint_value_raw} (before
normalization; used by the statistics of Module 4),
\code{endpoint_value_transformed} (e.g. after log10 for \code{"log_diff"}) and
\code{endpoint_value_norm} (normalized; used by the BMC of Module 5).
}

\section{Intra-plate vehicle-control QC}{

Following Truong et al. (2026, Section 2.6.2.2), plates whose VC larvae
behaved unusually are flagged; a person decides which to exclude:
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=detect_behavior_vc_baseline_outliers]{detect_behavior_vc_baseline_outliers()}}: per endpoint, plates
whose VC median (\code{denom}) lies outside a Tukey fence over all plates
(Q1 - 3 IQR, Q3 + 3 IQR by default).
\item Plates whose VC wells move inconsistently: movement-similarity
\code{denom} below a threshold (0.4 published), applied by the skill.
\item \code{\link[=summarize_behavior_vc_distribution]{summarize_behavior_vc_distribution()}} and
\code{\link[=plot_behavior_vc_baseline]{plot_behavior_vc_baseline()}} describe and show the baselines.
}
\code{\link[=validate_behavior_endpoints]{validate_behavior_endpoints()}} checks the structure of the endpoint
table (columns, unique keys, complete endpoints per well).
}

\section{Developmental toxicity endpoint}{

\code{\link[=calculate_devtox_endpoints]{calculate_devtox_endpoints()}} counts, per dose group, the larvae (\code{N},
wells present) and the affected larvae (\code{n_affected}, wells with
\code{keep_well = FALSE}: dead or malformed). This relies on the single-larva
well contract (\link{canonical-columns}); \code{N} may differ between dose groups.
\code{\link[=plot_devtox_dose_response_pages]{plot_devtox_dose_response_pages()}} plots percent affected. BMCs are
Module 5 (\link{bmc}).
